    "text": "A farmer <math><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has a land in the shape of a triangle with vertices at <math><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0, 0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1, 1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math> <mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2, 0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math> From this land, a neighbouring farmer <math><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> takes away the region which lies between the side <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> and a curve of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If the area of the region taken away by the farmer <math><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is exactly <math> <mrow> <mn>30%</mn> </mrow> </math> of the area of <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math> <mi>n</mi> </math> is",
